description:
Complete the save, outcome, lifecycle, variant, and legendary-economy semantics
for all 317 creatures.

Required membership — all of:
- every creature half-damage-on-success omission (plan states 79; a coarse
  whole-record scan of main @4384f25 gives 77 — the exact membership MUST be
  re-derived by the committed A2 clause predicate, not copied);
- multiple saves per entry, and save-ability alternatives (only the first save is
  typed today);
- trigger, duration, repeat, immunity, recovery, escape, secondary damage/check,
  and termination semantics;
- legendary-action budget and per-option costs;
- Frightful Presence, breath geometry, transformations, summoning, diseases,
  wounds, maximum-stat changes, and variant families;
- Avatar of Death and the inline stat-block gaps;
- conditional and rider damage typing — 14 of 771 creature damage clauses carry
  untyped riders (sneak attack extra dice, elk and hobgoblin riders, infernal
  wound, vampire sunlight 20 radiant) despite the readiness report claiming
  "mechanical prose: 0";
- exhaustive clause reconciliation beyond the earlier sampled surfaces.

Closes findings: F-25, F-26, F-32, F-33, SOL-006, CAP-004, Fable F3, and the
Opus residual "unverified effects semantics".
